title: The German October
subtitle: In Moscow the Politburo decides that the German revolution is near.
new-page: true
tags: event
view-if: year = 1923 and month = 9 and e23_october_path = 0 and crisis = 0
max-visits: 1
priority: 3
on-arrival: {!
if (!RG.e22) { this._runActions(this.game.scenes.e22_lib.onArrival); }
RG.e22.leader();
Q.e23_oct_directive = 0;
if (Q.comintern_member == 1) {
    // effort stays below what would close the directive by itself: the October's own end decides it
    RG.directive({
        id: 'october', title: 'The German October',
        text: 'The Executive instructs the German section to prepare the armed rising: to fix the date, to arm the proletarian hundreds, to enter the governments of Saxony and Thuringia as the base of the revolution, and to give the signal when the Reichswehr marches.',
        from: 'trotsky', months: 3,
        goals: [{q: 'e23_rising_phase', op: '=', v: 1}],
        reward: {funds: 3, favour: 20, faction: 'offensive'},
        punish: 'rival', announce: false
    });
    Q.e23_oct_directive = 1;
}
RG.news('German communist leaders summoned to Moscow', 2);
!}

= The German October

On 23 August, after the Cuno strike, the Politburo in Moscow decided that Germany is ripe. The German party is to prepare an armed rising, Moscow will pay for it, and Russian officers will help to plan it. [+ party_leader +] and the German leaders have spent September in Moscow.

Trotsky wants a date fixed in advance, as in Petrograd, and proposes 9 November. Brandler says the German party must choose the moment, and asks for Trotsky himself to come and lead it. Zinoviev wants a rising and is not sure he wants Trotsky to have the credit. [? if e23_patron = 2 : Trotsky has read every one of our reports since March, and it shows. ?][? if e23_patron = 3 : Radek, whom we have trusted since March, will be the Executive's man in Germany. ?]

The plan: the party enters the governments of Saxony and Thuringia, arms the hundreds from the state arsenals, and when the Reichswehr marches on Saxony a general strike becomes a rising across the Reich.

- @date: Accept the plan and Trotsky's date.
- @own_moment: Accept the plan, and keep the choice of the moment.
- @refuse: Refuse.

@date
subtitle: [? if lock_moscow_orders = 1 : Against the party line: costs Unity. ?] Money, rifles and Russian officers. Little room for our own judgement.
on-arrival: {!
RG.e22.against('moscow_orders');
RG.comply(25);
RG.ecci('trotsky', 10);
Q.comintern_rep = 'Karl Radek';
RG.setRole('radek', 'Envoy of the Executive, in Germany for the October');
RG.ledger('Accepted Moscow\'s plan for a German October, and Trotsky\'s date.', 'e23_plan');
Q.e23_october_path = 1;
Q.e23_date_set = 1;
Q.independence -= 10;
Q.resources += 3;
Q.red_guards_arms += (Q.e23_patron == 2 ? 10 : 6);
Q.lean_offensive += 2;
!}

The date is set and written in no document. Pyatakov and Radek leave for Berlin with false papers. Red Army officers follow, and a great deal of money.

@own_moment
subtitle: Moscow's help on German terms. Trotsky is annoyed.
on-arrival: {!
RG.comply(15);
RG.ecci('trotsky', -6);
RG.ecci('radek', 5);
Q.comintern_rep = 'Karl Radek';
RG.setRole('radek', 'Envoy of the Executive, in Germany for the October');
RG.ledger('Accepted Moscow\'s plan for a German October, on German terms.', 'e23_plan');
Q.e23_october_path = 1;
Q.e23_date_set = 0;
Q.independence -= 4;
Q.resources += (Q.e23_patron == 3 ? 3 : 2);
Q.red_guards_arms += 4;
Q.lean_unionist += 2;
!}

Moscow agrees that the Germans will give the signal. Trotsky is not sent. Radek and Pyatakov are, with a group of Red Army officers to plan the military side.

@refuse
subtitle: The German working class is not ready for power. Moscow's money and patience run out.
on-arrival: {!
RG.defy();
RG.ecci('zinoviev', -10);
RG.ecci('trotsky', -10);
RG.ecci('radek', 4);
Q.e23_october_path = 0;
Q.e23_october_refused = 1;
Q.independence += 10;
Q.moscow_subsidy = Math.max(0, Q.moscow_subsidy - 1);
Q.offensive_satisfaction -= 12;
Q.lean_luxemburgist += 3;
RG.ledger('Refused Moscow\'s plan for a rising in October 1923.', 'e23_plan');
!}

[? if luxemburg_alive = 1 : Rosa Luxemburg writes the German reply. A revolution, she writes, cannot be ordered for a date like a delivery of coal. ?][? if luxemburg_alive = 0 : The German delegation says no, politely and then less politely. ?] Zinoviev calls it the gravest error since Levi. Radek, in private, is relieved.
